%T A145604 1201,1401,1738
%N A145604 Number of pairs of consecutive integers x, x+1 such that both are prime(n)-smooth but both are not prime(n-1)-smooth.
%C A145604 See A145605 for a triangle of x value. See A145606 for the largest x for each n.
%C A145604 An effective abc conjecture (c < rad(abc)^2) would imply that a(20)-a(33) is (943, 1201, 1401, 1738, 1955, 2240, 2793, 3340, 3860, 4582, 5284, 6050, 6883, 7984). - _Lucas A. Brown_, Oct 16 2022
%C A145604 a(20)-a(23) are proven unconditionally (see link): they are the first differences of A002071(19..23), with a(22) and a(23) of A002071 computed without assuming GRH or the abc conjecture. They agree with the abc-conditional values above. - _Jennifer Voitle_, Oct 28 2026
